{
  "reviews": {
    "node-1jcxq0c": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims 'it does not prove every supply disturbance appears in the sample export.' The evidence (IA-P01) explicitly states: 'The export supplies these sampled values, not a continuous waveform' and 'does not include data from all locations or valve states'. This directly supports the limitation. However, the node's detail also claims IA-P02 maps AL-44 to H-R(P-R). The evidence for this mapping exists in claim-1hxmwwu (IA-P02), but the specific text 'PR-12 maps it to... not C-11' is found there. The issue with node-1jcxq0c is that its detail conflates two separate points: 1) AL-44 mapping (supported by IA-P02 excerpt in claim-af3ts9), and 2) the limitation of sample exports (supported by IA-P01). While both parts are supported, the node's label 'it does not prove every supply disturbance...' is a valid conclusion from IA-P01. The proposed status 'supported' should be retained if we accept that the *entire* detail text must be fully substantiated. Let's re-read: 'IA-P02 states PR-12 maps AL-44 to H-R (P-R) and that this mapping is for instrumentation only.' This specific sentence about IA-P02 stating it does not guarantee all disturbances are logged is NOT in the provided evidence packet. The evidence packet has IA-P01 saying 'The export supplies these sampled values, not a continuous waveform' but no text from IA-P02 explicitly says 'the register does not establish valve state or guarantee all disturbances are logged'. Therefore, part of the detail lacks direct source support.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A passage from IA-P02 that states: 'The point register maps AL-44 to H-R (P-R) and this mapping is for instrumentation only. It also notes the register does not establish valve state or guarantee all disturbances are logged.'",
      "question": "Does any record in the evidence packet contain text stating that IA-P02 explicitly notes 'the register does not establish valve state or guarantee all disturbances are logged'?"
    },
    "node-aoyj0l": {
      "supported": true,
      "issue": "",
      "evidenceNeeded": "",
      "question": ""
    },
    "node-xkjnfv": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims 'No line opening was authorized at the time of notification.' The evidence (IA-S01 log entry) states: 'No line opening authorized' at 10:02. This supports the claim that no authorization existed *at that moment*. However, the detail says 'This indicates a procedural control... remained in place'. While true, this is an interpretation of what 'no line opening authorized' implies (i.e., isolation/authorization was still required). The evidence does not explicitly state that a procedural control 'remained in place', only that no authorization existed. This distinction matters for causal analysis: the absence of authorization doesn't automatically mean controls were active; it just means they weren't bypassed yet.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A record stating that at 10:02, an isolation or procedural control was actively in place (not merely absent), OR a statement clarifying what 'No line opening authorized' implies about the status of controls.",
      "question": "Does any evidence explicitly state that at 10:02, an active isolation/procedural control existed alongside the lack of authorization?"
    }
  },
  "decision": {
    "summary": "Two nodes require revision due to unsupported claims in their details. Node-1jcxq0c relies on a specific sentence from IA-P02 that is not present in the evidence packet; only general limitations about sample exports are supported by IA-P01. Node-xkjnfv conflates 'no authorization' with an active procedural control, which requires explicit textual support to be considered fully verified.",
    "evidenceUsed": ["IA-S01_shift_and_notification_log.md", "fcd254db-75b3-4a9d-abec-44c5b6a9b34e#1 (IA-P01)", "da0260c0-7d49-43e8-b074-da2a14c7d59c#1 (IA-P02)"],
    "unknowns": ["Whether IA-P02 contains the specific text about not guaranteeing all disturbances are logged", "What 'No line opening authorized' implies regarding active procedural controls at 10:02"],
    "alternatives": [
      "Accept partial support for node-1jcxq0c if we separate its two claims (AL-44 mapping vs. export limitation) and verify them independently.",
      "Rephrase node-xkjnfv to focus solely on the absence of authorization without implying active controls unless supported."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.85
  }
}
